From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ahtsiu <ahtsiu@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: mv64xxx: pin controller active to break runtime-PM deadlock

On Allwinner boards where the PMIC sits on the r_i2c bus (e.g. H618 with
AXP313A), a CPU DVFS transition deadlocks: cpufreq holds clk_prepare_lock
while writing the PMIC voltage, the I2C host resume path needs the same
lock, and the MMC runtime suspend worker waits on it too. The controller
ends up wedged ("I2C bus locked") and CPU0 stops answering NMIs.

Keep the controller runtime-resumed for as long as the driver is bound,
which removes the resume/suspend path that participates in the deadlock.
Same approach as Armbian's drv-i2c-busses-mv64xxx-pin-runtime-pm patch.

Signed-off-by: ahtsiu <ahtsiu@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-mv64xxx.c
@@ -149,6 +149,7 @@
 	bool			clk_n_base_0;
 	struct i2c_bus_recovery_info	rinfo;
 	bool			atomic;
+	bool			rtpm_pinned;
 };
 
 static struct mv64xxx_i2c_regs mv64xxx_i2c_regs_mv64xxx = {
@@ -1045,6 +1046,13 @@
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(&pd->dev, MSEC_PER_SEC);
 	pm_runtime_use_autosuspend(&pd->dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(&pd->dev);
+	/* Pin device active while bound to avoid circular PM deadlock */
+	rc = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pd->dev);
+	if (rc < 0) {
+		dev_warn(&pd->dev, "failed to resume during probe: %d\n", rc);
+		goto exit_disable_pm;
+	}
+	drv_data->rtpm_pinned = true;
 	if (!pm_runtime_enabled(&pd->dev)) {
 		rc = mv64xxx_i2c_runtime_resume(&pd->dev);
 		if (rc)
@@ -1069,6 +1077,8 @@
 exit_free_irq:
 	free_irq(drv_data->irq, drv_data);
 exit_disable_pm:
+	if (drv_data->rtpm_pinned)
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pd->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pd->dev);
 	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pd->dev))
 		mv64xxx_i2c_runtime_suspend(&pd->dev);
@@ -1083,6 +1093,8 @@
 
 	i2c_del_adapter(&drv_data->adapter);
 	free_irq(drv_data->irq, drv_data);
+	if (drv_data->rtpm_pinned)
+		pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pd->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pd->dev);
 	if (!pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pd->dev))
 		mv64xxx_i2c_runtime_suspend(&pd->dev);
